    I'd like to take a moment to acknowledge a few people and comment on a
few things...

    First of all, the response I've gotten towards this game has been
absolutely unbelievable! :-) From those who remembered playing this game in
the past, to those who had played it on other computer platforms, to those
who had never heard of the game, but got "hooked" after playing it a few
times! Over the past few weeks(the current lifespan of this game), I've
received over 200 emails pertaining to just this one game! Unbelievable!

    I'd also like to THANK numerous people for their testing efforts and
ESPECIALLY for their INFORMATIVE bug reports. 90% of the reports given to
me have contained enough info for me to zero in on the bad code within a
matter of minutes!

    One of the requests I've been getting a LOT of is to convert the game
into a "real" multi-player version, allowing port to port playing. I would
most definately like to see this added to the game sometime in the future,
however it seems like MOST of the games I've put out in recent years could
benefit greatly by having this feature added(like in YachtZee & AceyDeucey
to name others). Wheel of Fortune already has this feature(in the Registered
version), so I already KNOW how to do it, however it takes a fair chunk of
time to make the needed conversions to the existing coding. Eventually, I'll
get around to creating multi-port versions of other games, however I'd like
to spend my present time working on other ventures.

